BE-293: a failed IdentityHub credential await must set the BPNL_CREDENTIAL / MEMBERSHIP_CREDENTIAL entry FAILED

Base: ARENA2036/portal-backend 274096a965c10d65a96d8c077a60b7680176aff7 (fix/BE-293-retrigger-validate-did-in-progress,
admin image on Alpha). IdentityHubCredentialAwaitBusinessLogic.cs is identical in ad459ee7 (other images on Alpha).

Defect: AWAIT_BPN_CREDENTIAL_RESPONSE / AWAIT_MEMBERSHIP_CREDENTIAL_RESPONSE returned ProcessStepStatusId.FAILED with
ModifyChecklistEntry = null, both when the IdentityHub reports the holder request as ERROR and when the wait
deadline passes. The executor therefore left the checklist entry IN_PROGRESS while scheduling
RETRIGGER_REQUEST_*_CREDENTIAL; the manual retrigger (RegistrationBusinessLogic.TriggerChecklistInternal) requires
the entry in FAILED and answered 409, so the application could not be recovered through the API.
Fix: both terminal branches set the entry FAILED with a non-sensitive comment (credential name and configured wait
only), mirroring ApplicationChecklistService.HandleServiceErrorAsync. Retrigger scheduling, ISSUED (DONE), pending
(TODO, entry untouched) and the deadline comparison are unchanged.

Persistence: ApplicationChecklistProcessTypeExecutor applies ModifyChecklistEntry through
AttachAndModifyApplicationChecklist; ProcessExecutor/ProcessExecutionService then save step status, checklist entry,
the new retrigger step and the process version in one SaveAsync (one transaction) per step.

Affected image: portal-processes-worker only (ApplicationChecklistHandlerService is the only caller). Administration
and Registration reference the library for DI but never run the await handlers. Migrations, schema: unchanged.
An application already in the mismatch state (await FAILED, entry IN_PROGRESS) is NOT repaired by this change.

Tests: 16 new/extended cases fail on the old code and pass with the fix (IdentityHub.Library.Tests 68/68,
ApplicationChecklist.Executor.Tests 51/51, ApplicationChecklist.Library.Tests 37/37, IssuerComponent.Library.Tests
38/38, Administration.Service.Tests 788/792 - the 4 failures are Testcontainers integration tests without Docker).

Apply: git apply --index ci/portal-backend-identityhub-await-checklist-failed.patch   (from the portal-backend root)

